# Styling Rules

## CSS Architecture
The library has two styling layers:

1. **`src/styles/tableStyles.css`** — Scoped component CSS, wrapped in `@layer rtbl { ... }` to prevent cascade conflicts with consumer styles. All selectors use the `rtbl-` prefix.
2. **Tailwind utility classes** — Applied inline in JSX for dynamic, state-driven styles (dark mode, hover, responsive).

## `@layer rtbl` Requirement
All rules in `tableStyles.css` MUST live inside `@layer rtbl { ... }`. Never add bare/global rules.

Reason: CSS Cascade Layers (`@layer`) ensure library styles have lower specificity than any unlayered consumer styles, so the library never wins a specificity war.

## `rtbl-` Prefix
Every class defined in `tableStyles.css` MUST start with `rtbl-`. This prevents naming collisions with consumer CSS frameworks or component libraries.

## Never `@import` Third-Party CSS Here
`@import "react-loading-skeleton/dist/skeleton.css"` was intentionally removed.
The skeleton CSS is loaded by `TableSkeleton.tsx` via a JS import, which only runs when the component is actually rendered.
Do NOT re-add any `@import` of third-party CSS to `tableStyles.css` — it would bundle those styles into `dist/index.css` unconditionally.

## Tailwind Config (`tailwind.config.js`)
- `preflight: false` — disables Tailwind's CSS reset to avoid affecting consumer pages
- Content paths scan only `./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}` — do not widen this

## Dark Mode in Tailwind
The library uses class-based dark mode via `isDarkMode` state + `.dark` class on the container.
CSS dark variants target `.rtbl-container.dark .rtbl-*`.
Tailwind dark utilities (`dark:bg-gray-700`) work because `enableDarkMode` adds `.dark` to the container class.

## Consumer Setup (Tailwind v3)
Consumers must add the library to their `content` array for Tailwind to scan its classes:
```js
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  content: [
    "./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}",
    "./node_modules/nextjs-reusable-table/dist/**/*.{js,mjs}",
  ],
};
```

## Consumer Setup (Tailwind v4)
```css
/* globals.css */
@import "tailwindcss";
@source "../node_modules/nextjs-reusable-table/dist";
```
